edb/ref 1031 "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050189 #edb/ref 1033 3357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050189 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "34f05255-901a-5db2-9431-e0175ef37691" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186168610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186168611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186168612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186168613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186168614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186168613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168609 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2431be4b-89af-5247-a309-422a67c531ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168610 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168610 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168610 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8aec1b3a-f253-5279-99f6-12a688430707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168611 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168611 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168611 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "acbd015f-0d6c-538b-9f05-45ee71f8c513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168612 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168612 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168612 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d8e6ebd5-405c-535f-9ceb-b01c692d8bcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168613 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168613 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168613 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53f9ce92-f40b-51c9-86f1-dceb0bbaeb93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168614 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168614 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168614 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "76624ec5-45cd-5b6f-a504-2ff12623de24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171856 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171856 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](images/ef/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171856 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8cbffe56-0a93-59c5-9ea8-c4040e07bb03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171856 #edb/ref 1074 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/d4/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171857 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8684" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171857 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](images/b8/b8e630b749cbfee41d73a620ffd284f3216bb8a43affdc26543f1eb57e4613c5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "053b6396-341c-5b1f-a942-ca1fbf6efa7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171857 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171897 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171897 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171897 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb87998f-3236-510b-94aa-7db80487d8c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171897 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Connected Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172050 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172051 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172091 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1045 "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186172912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172179 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "39f4cc17-5f7c-50ed-be96-16f8865ff40e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186168609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (1,1)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,2x-y\\ne 0\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8379be09-e532-538d-bf76-16e36177bb9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172291 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(1,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186461116 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186461117 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186461118 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186461119 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98036" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/00/0045eda99f40f774d2ef21214522eebb0c53bffee304ba503a9076a7491cc648.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72da8c2e-5747-5cf0-addd-5e327ef519dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172669 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains two holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172912 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172912 #edb/ref 1061 32029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172912 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "201490fd-cd86-52ab-9247-93c541739d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172912 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172922 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172922 #edb/ref 1061 32247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172922 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c68b13ae-8c87-5be9-86e9-3707d272d31a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172922 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172923 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172923 #edb/ref 1061 32249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172923 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f9dde17-161c-5a88-8c63-6a5f3ee9022f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172923 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172968 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172968 #edb/ref 1061 34472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172968 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bbce5649-95d6-5507-989b-451ad6e19fa2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172968 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173000 #edb/ref 1061 35576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173000 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b521866b-f579-55ce-87fd-6140979c0866" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173000 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173164 #edb/ref 1064 "A region $D$ is **connected** if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path that lies entirely in $D.$\n\nThe region below is connected because a smooth path can join any two points.\n\n![](images/90/90fea89e0dabec960edf7eef3552e10cdbccaee80f9ef6ca3d5b2a5b457e6b89.png)\n\nThe region below is not connected. If we take two points $P$ and $Q,$ one in each subregion, we cannot find a path joining these points that lies entirely in the region.\n\n![](images/08/08cd555c38106ec22f2ffe4808a6b62e8f72ffda7baf953836beeca5ee6a1faf.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173164 #edb/ref 1065 5105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173164 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cc905518-dd4e-5791-9cf9-5655233a30a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173164 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173189 #edb/ref 1064 "A connected region $D$ is **simply connected** if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nWhen we have a connected *plane* region (e.g. a region in the $xy$-plane), determining whether it's simply connected is a little simpler: we just need to check whether the region contains holes. \n\nPlane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nSo, if a connected plane region does not contain any holes, then it is simply connected.\n\nMore precisely, a connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173189 #edb/ref 1065 5574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173189 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a2c2be37-32a5-5b2c-8386-ef9e32684998" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173189 #edb/ref 1067 "Simply-Connected Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257203 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ae/ae77eaad51b8cd6bff4e62032946254da948e7643b45bd5e3a2343462ac457cb.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257203 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257203 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2fd295e1-1f3f-51b0-a531-01895286cbb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257297 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ba/ba9b18a202db25c02b0907665d24fca75c9f4afc5babe898ff8f9c0227c7d447.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257297 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257297 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a04266f-fa97-5bc9-a110-7f2c8e8f9f80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257541 #edb/ref 1080 "images/82/82a33d59ae0060b0f1187415698ccf36ae45bd4ddc1fce0af74d01df74356ee1.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257541 #edb/ref 1083 