 is *not* connected?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259573 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "856afbeb-9f59-56e5-affb-452bd8050ce2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259573 #edb/ref 1074 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png)\n\n \n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/2b/2bcaaf15d709d6396155bcdc9e8976bb037c9f341fc0b8863687958dbb0f40ff.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123885" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de4d0c85-6915-5695-9beb-a379a8504775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259574 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following: \n\n![](images/4a/4a67c845fe7993fe0c91784c92201db6ff5c15098db04dc588f5ebe0e8cdc1a1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462817 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462818 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462819 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (2,1)}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>25}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "beac61f6-0d9e-58bf-85d2-405f0693eb4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259578 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn. \n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(2,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 25.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462823 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462824 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462825 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+x\\ne 0}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "387d1688-e72e-5fdc-bd02-55d9c19c099b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259730 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge x.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole (containing all points of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1$).\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=-x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462826 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462827 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462828 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124782" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd4c2e21-ea3a-5149-9740-8c2a599beff2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259731 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\n- Region II  is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected.  The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the coordinate axes.  Thus, the region is formed by four disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186460499 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592